From 38cbd954b824f36a25318863f16e7a9ec58d95ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vfhiyl <VfhiyL@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:34:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Load only the module built with Immich's libvips

sharp loads its native module from src/build/Release when it was built from source, and otherwise from prebuilt packages (@img/sharp-*), which bring their own libvips. Immich builds libvips and sharp's module itself (native/build.sh), with the formats and changes it needs, and server/bin/install-native puts the module in src/build/Release. sharp now loads only that one, and fails with a message saying how to install it, instead of falling back to a prebuilt module.

sharp.versions gives the versions of the libraries built in, from the versions.json installed with the module. HEIC is read too (the prebuilt modules of sharp read only AVIF).
---
 dist/sharp.cjs   | 153 +++--------------------------------------------
 dist/sharp.mjs   | 153 +++--------------------------------------------
 dist/utility.cjs |  26 ++------
 dist/utility.mjs |  26 ++------
 4 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 336 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dist/sharp.cjs b/dist/sharp.cjs
index bea6c6a..033f152 100644
--- a/dist/sharp.cjs
+++ b/dist/sharp.cjs
@@ -20,155 +20,16 @@ const runtimePlatform = runtimePlatformArch();
 /* node:coverage disable */
 
